=== WEB SOURCE ANALYSIS ===
The web DigitalTwinPage (181 lines) is a live, single-vehicle physical-state screen: a main
visualization panel (the `<VehicleTwin>` illustration + `<VehiclePaintPicker>` + last-updated
caption) beside three read-only detail panels (Doors, Windows, Security & Status), with a
vehicle selector in the PageContainer actions slot and a 5s `REFRESH_INTERVAL` poll.
The parity-manifest record scopes this unit to:
  dataSources : useVehicles, useVehicleState, useSecurityLatest, useChargingTelemetryLatest
  panels      : GlassPanel1..GlassPanel5  (no-vehicles · visualization · doors · windows · security)
  charts/maps : none
  states      : loading, empty, success  (+ error for robustness)
  strings     : 37  (8 common.* + 29 digitalTwin.*)
  requiredCount: 45  (5 panels + 3 states + 37 strings)
The three live feeds merge into one VehicleTwinState via `buildTwinState` (the page's
`twinState` memo) — the doors/windows/security rows and the illustration both read from it.
The badge resolves a single source-of-truth status (web `badgeStatus`): twin charging/driving
win, else `deriveVehicleStatus(state)`, else a live signal collapses offline→online.

The Swift port REUSES the canonical module twin domain rather than re-deriving it (ADR-004,
predecessor reuse): `TwinStateBuilder.buildTwinState` (the verbatim port of lib/vehicleState.ts),
`VehicleTwinState` + the window/door/turn enums + `Twin{Security,VehicleState,Charging}Input`,
the shared Canvas illustration `VehicleTwinView`, and the `VehiclePaintPicker` shared surface
(+ `InMemoryVehiclePaintStore`). All four web hook names are kept verbatim at the Swift call sites.

